# Job Hunter AI — Cursor Project Rules

Follow these documents as source of truth (in order):

1. `docs/MASTER_PROMPT.md`
2. `docs/CURSOR_RULES.md`
3. `docs/RULES.md`
4. `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
5. Relevant domain docs (`docs/DATABASE.md`, `docs/AI.md`, `docs/PLAYWRIGHT.md`, `docs/SCRAPERS.md`, `docs/ATS.md`)

Company seed data: `docs/companies-to-work/`.

## Non-negotiables

- Clean Architecture: Presentation → Application → Domain ← Infrastructure
- Never put business logic in pages or React components
- Never use `any`; TypeScript strict only
- Always use DTOs, Repository Pattern, Service/Use Case layer, Zod validation
- Components ≤ 300 lines; files ≤ 500 lines
- Document exported functions
- UI: shadcn/ui, Tailwind, dark mode, desktop-first, pt-BR + en
- Playwright only via reusable browser services; no hardcoded brittle selectors in use cases
- Prefer complete, production-ready implementations over stubs
- Update `docs/TODO.md` when behavior or backlog changes
- Do not commit secrets; do not push/PR unless asked
